# openapi-spectral-rules

This is `@trimble-oss/openapi-spectral-rules`: deterministic Spectral lint rules for Trimble OpenAPI specs. Not a UI app. Ignore Modus / web-component guidance.

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing rules.

## Commands

- Install / test: `npm ci` then `npm test` (Node `>=18`; npm only)
- Smoke lint: `npm run lint-petstore-v3`
- Versioned lint: `npm run lint-auto -- <file>` or `--ruleset spectral-r2023.1.yaml` / `spectral-r2026.1.yaml`

## Source of truth

- Canonical rules: `spectral.yaml` (tags `R2023.1` / `R2026.1`)
- Entrypoints: `spectral-r2026.1.yaml` (all on), `spectral-r2023.1.yaml` (r2026-only rules `off`)
- Custom functions: CommonJS in `functions/`
- Tests: Jest + `linterForRule` in `test/utils.js`

Do not treat `spectral-ruleset.json` or `api-spec-ruleset.json` as editable sources.

## Hard boundary

Do not implement semantic/LLM checks here (`tas-semantic-*`). Those belong in the LLM validation pipeline (platform-ai-kit).
